model g6_refusal_order_twin
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
  note "T, issue #55, G6: which refusal a place keeps (E §4.1, E §4.2 step 4; tally 2.1.2's text order, #57 asks the spec): the twin of g6/refusal_order: a's leg goes into gone after its lifespan ends (RUN-LIFESPAN), ab's into keep, alive, so a.cash is the one refusal at src and bal(src) prints it."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money DUK

input d0: date

place src: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place gone: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..2025-01-05

place keep: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

move a: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from src to gone amount amt

move ab: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from src to keep amount amt

ask q: bal(src, 2025-01-31)

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 1.00 DUK
  d0 = 2025-01-10
  opening[src] = 500.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[gone] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[keep] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
